      "content": "Given that utilization is low and the spikes appear random, a physical layer issue like marginal cabling or a failing transceiver is certainly a possibility to check. It could also be related to software-level events on the core router, such as resource contention or periodic garbage collection that causes brief processing delays. Try running diagnostics specifically on the upstream link interfaces to check for CRC errors or interface flapping logs.",
